# oracle: fix npt/cauchy continue across two runs on NiAlH_jea eam/alloy, 3x3x3 fcc (108 atoms) prism box as in the LAMMPS example in.cauchystat (second run adds an xy tilt target -10000 bar and continue yes); 2 x 100 steps; thermo every 20 steps. Native: installed lmp (b332f28, EXTRA-FIX included).
# Measured with native LAMMPS: this engine agrees with the native run to a max relative error of 2.3e-12 (thermo, row 6 pxz) and 2.4e-12 (per-atom, scaled by max(1,|value|)); the continuation run (xy target -10000, continue yes) is part of the match.
# oracle-potentials: NiAlH_jea.eam.alloy
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map array
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 4.05
region          simbox prism 0 3 0 3 0 3 0 0 0 units lattice
create_box      2 simbox
create_atoms    2 box
mass            1 58.69
mass            2 26.98154
pair_style      eam/alloy
pair_coeff      * * NiAlH_jea.eam.alloy Ni Al
neigh_modify    delay 5
timestep        0.002
fix             1 all npt/cauchy temp 600.0 600.0 1.0 x 0.0 0.0 0.1 y 0.0 0.0 0.1 z 0.0 0.0 0.1 couple none alpha 0.001 continue no
thermo_style    custom step temp pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz lx ly lz xy xz yz pe f_1
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          20
velocity        all create 1200 4928459 rot yes dist gaussian loop geom
run             100
fix             1 all npt/cauchy temp 600.0 600.0 1.0 x 0.0 0.0 0.1 y 0.0 0.0 0.1 z 0.0 0.0 0.1 xy -10000.0 -10000.0 0.1 couple none alpha 0.001 continue yes
run             100
